Title: Lock the object table mutex instead of only unlocking it
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: doc::Object::id(), Object::setId() and doc::get_object() guard the global object table with base::scoped_unlock, which only unlocks the mutex when it goes out of scope. The mutex is never locked, so the table is unprotected against other threads, and every call unlocks a mutex nobody holds (undefined behaviour). Linux ignores it; AROS raises "Semaphore in an illegal state" (seen on the first stroke on the canvas, from ExpandCelCanvas::commit via PatchCel/WithCel).
Change: Use base::scoped_lock, which locks in its constructor and unlocks in its destructor.
Scope: all platforms
Upstream: candidate
Verification: found with a diagnostic build that reports unlocks of mutexes the caller does not hold (tests/aros/unlock-check.c), mainline x86_64, pool v1-1, 2026-11-16
Removal: when upstream uses scoped_lock there.
---
diff --git a/src/doc/object.cpp b/src/doc/object.cpp
index cd3909e22856d380125f8e45861df5f8366094e9..846658cab39514de62324c62e44eb8fc712c4442 100644
--- a/src/doc/object.cpp
+++ b/src/doc/object.cpp
@@ -53,7 +53,7 @@ const ObjectId Object::id() const
   // The first time the ID is request, we store the object in the
   // "objects" hash table.
   if (!m_id) {
-    base::scoped_unlock hold(mutex);
+    base::scoped_lock hold(mutex);
     m_id = ++newId;
     objects.insert(std::make_pair(m_id, const_cast<Object*>(this)));
   }
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@ const ObjectId Object::id() const
 
 void Object::setId(ObjectId id)
 {
-  base::scoped_unlock hold(mutex);
+  base::scoped_lock hold(mutex);
 
   if (m_id) {
     auto it = objects.find(m_id);
@@ -87,7 +87,7 @@ void Object::setVersion(ObjectVersion version)
 
 Object* get_object(ObjectId id)
 {
-  base::scoped_unlock hold(mutex);
+  base::scoped_lock hold(mutex);
   auto it = objects.find(id);
   if (it != objects.end())
     return it->second;
